3b:["$","section",null,{"className":"mb-16","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-display text-3xl font-bold mb-8","children":"Frequently Asked Questions"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-6","children":[["$","div","0",{"className":"p-6 rounded-2xl border border-border/50 bg-card","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-lg mb-3","children":"How do I know which mantra is right for me?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed","children":"Consider your deity preference, your predominant yoga path (Bhakti/Jnana/Karma), and which mantra creates a sense of resonance when you hear it. The tradition says the right mantra produces a feeling of 'coming home.'"}]]}],["$","div","1",{"className":"p-6 rounded-2xl border border-border/50 bg-card","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-lg mb-3","children":"Is it better to receive a mantra or choose one yourself?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed","children":"Ideally both: choose a mantra that resonates, then seek guidance from a qualified teacher (Guru) for formal initiation (Diksha). An initiated mantra is said to carry the energetic lineage of all previous practitioners."}]]}],["$","div","2",{"className":"p-6 rounded-2xl border border-border/50 bg-card","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-lg mb-3","children":"Can I use multiple mantras?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed","children":"Beginners are generally advised to pick one and stick with it for at least 40 days before exploring others. The power of a mantra builds with consistent, deep practice — not variety."}]]}],["$","div","3",{"className":"p-6 rounded-2xl border border-border/50 bg-card","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-lg mb-3","children":"What is a Beeja Mantra?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed","children":"A Beeja (seed) mantra is a single-syllable sound that carries concentrated energy: Om, Hreem, Kleem, Aim, Shreem. They are the most compact and potent form of mantra, and are often embedded within longer mantras."}]]}],["$","div","4",{"className":"p-6 rounded-2xl border border-border/50 bg-card","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-lg mb-3","children":"What mantra is best for anxiety?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed","children":"So'ham ('I am That') and Om Shanti (peace) are widely used for anxiety. Pranava Om repeated slowly is deeply calming. The Maha Mrityunjaya Mantra is specifically prescribed for fear and health concerns."}]]}],["$","div","5",{"className":"p-6 rounded-2xl border border-border/50 bg-card","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-lg mb-3","children":"Do I need to understand Sanskrit to use mantras?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed","children":"No, but understanding the meaning deepens the practice. Mantras work through sound vibration — the precise pronunciation matters more than conceptual understanding, especially initially."}]]}],["$","div","6",{"className":"p-6 rounded-2xl border border-border/50 bg-card","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-lg mb-3","children":"What mantra is best for someone on the Jnana path?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed","children":"Aham Brahmasmi ('I am Brahman') or So'ham ('I am That') are the Mahavakyas most aligned with the Jnana path. They are less devotional and more directly pointed at the nature of the self."}]]}],["$","div","7",{"className":"p-6 rounded-2xl border border-border/50 bg-card","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-lg mb-3","children":"Can children practice mantra?"}],"$L42"]}]]}]]}]
